IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC, phase 1: the fork form.
--
-- `UPON EACH` is the fork: the continuation fires once PER tenant who
-- pays, independently, rather than once when all have (spec §2.2.6, §3.2).
-- The join is a line of its own between the act's WITHIN and the HENCE
-- (R-Q1, RULED 2026-09-07). The fork's words were ruled `UPON EACH` the same
-- day: a barrier is level-triggered and fires once, a fork is edge-triggered and
-- fires per completion, so the trigger lives in the keyword rather than in a
-- threshold. `ONCE EACH HAS` no longer parses.
--
-- `amount`, bound by the action pattern, and `t`, bound by EVERY, are both in
-- scope in the continuation and in LEST. The inner obligation is parenthesised,
-- as the corpus writes every nested obligation: it has no closing token, so its
-- own optional HENCE/LEST would otherwise swallow the outer LEST.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each payment gets a receipt` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Pay (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY theLandlord) amount
        WITHIN 7
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord
                    MUST   Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY amount)
                    WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH BY t
